                <pb facs="1349" n="1309" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p1/pg1309"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">885.211/9–1153: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 663<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in
                        Syria</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d663-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-09-11T19:53:00-04:00">September 11, 1953—7:53
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>95. In anticipation General Bennike’s having to make decision soon after
                    September 15 on Israel’s attempt to divert Jordan and in understanding that he
                    may wish indication of support from US, you may inform him of following: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>US is of view that Article 5 of Armistice Agreement formally
                            establishes UN Chairman of ISMAC, and not Israel or Syria, as
                            responsible party for general supervision and administration of
                            demilitarized zone. This authority has been acquiesced in by both
                            parties. This situation remains until Israel and Syria reach agreement
                            to contrary or armistice agreement is modified. US took this position in
                            SC debate on Huleh dispute in May 1951. It will reiterate this position
                            as often as necessary.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>We are prepared in absence full details in this incident of damming
                            Jordan to assure him of US general support in any decision he may make
                            within his authority since we are firmly of conviction MAC machinery
                            must have adequate backing to assure effective enforcement of Armistice
                            Agreements.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d663-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d663-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to Jerusalem as telegram 18, to New York as 118, and to Tel Aviv as
                    204.</p>
